One could think of data science as art grounded in facts. It tells a story through visualization. Both story and visualization rely on a good plot. And there are plenty to choose from, many with their own Wikipedia page {{< iconify iconoir emoji-surprise-alt >}}.

Which attract the most readers? How has that attention changed over time? Let’s build a Shiny app to explore their daily page views. These tell us something about attention to the articles, rather than how often people actually use each chart.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
library(dplyr)
library(ggplot2)
library(lubridate)
library(purrr)
library(stringr)
library(tibble)
library(shiny)
library(bslib)
library(rvest)
library(scales)
library(httr2)
library(wesanderson)
```
:::





